BearSSL subset vendored for the experimental BBP auth2 verifier.

Upstream: https://www.bearssl.org/git/BearSSL
Commit: 7bea48e5e850ab4cafbe68d3765cdaba13a86d6f
Imported: 2026-08-25
License: MIT; see LICENSE.txt and the notice in every imported source file.
Integrity: SHA256SUMS records every imported upstream file; verify from the
repository root with `make auth2-vendor-check`.

The imported file-level closure contains the public headers, SHA-256 small
implementation, P-256 m15 implementation, raw ECDSA i15 verifier, required
curve definitions, i15 arithmetic, and codec helpers. Upstream files are
unmodified. The generic raw verifier directly references P-384/P-521 tables and
the shared hash source also emits SHA-224 code; those internals remain linked
but are not accepted by the BearBoot wrapper. BearBoot redirects memory calls
to private freestanding symbols and localizes all BearSSL/provider symbols in
the final relocatable object. Only the three `bbp_auth2_*` public API functions
remain global.

This pin has no signed upstream release or tag. Updating it requires recording a
new exact commit, reviewing the selected closure and license, running the
freestanding unresolved/exported-symbol and x86 SIMD audits, all auth2 vectors,
sanitizers, and the complete host gate. The repository exposes no generic
BearSSL API and does not ship this Draft surface in SDK 1.4.0.
